# name: test/sql/reader_registry_git.test
# description: a git:// URI's reader, with duck_tails loaded to parse its revision (#148)
# group: [sql]

#
# WHY THIS FILE LOADS duck_tails. panduck has no git grammar of its own (#148, stage 2):
# ExtOfPath hands a git:// path to the VFS, duck_tails' CanonicalizePath moves an `@rev`
# into `?ref=` (duck_tails#68, shipped in 1.9.0), and the `?ref=` cut leaves the path.
# reader_registry.test runs without duck_tails and so sees only the as-written path. This
# file is the half that sees the canonical one.
#
# THESE ASSERTIONS PIN THE SERVED duck_tails, not a panduck commit. Written against
# duck_tails 1.9.0 (2b20b7d); any duck_tails with the CanonicalizePath override
# (duck_tails#68) gives the same answers. If this file goes red with no panduck
# commit, check what the community registry serves for duck_tails first.
#
# UNGATED. duck_tails excludes only the wasm platforms, and CI builds the wasm extension
# but never runs this suite on it (MainDistributionPipeline.yml, wasm-symbol-check).

require panduck

statement ok
INSTALL duck_tails FROM community;

statement ok
LOAD duck_tails;

# THE ACCEPTANCE CASES FROM #148. A reflog revision is one revision: duck_tails takes the
# last `@` not followed by `{`. StripGitRevision, the copy stage 2 deleted, cut at the last
# `@` and answered NULL for both (#147).
query II
SELECT panduck_format_for('git://a.md@HEAD@{0}')         AS reflog,
       panduck_format_for('git://a.md@main@{1.day.ago}') AS reflog_date;
----
markdown	markdown

# The deprecated form keeps its reader through duck_tails, with no copy in panduck.
query II
SELECT panduck_format_for('git://a.md@HEAD')        AS at_rev,
       panduck_format_for('git://docs/Doc.md@12345') AS nested_rev;
----
markdown	markdown

# AN `@` IN THE NAME AND AN `@rev` AFTER IT. duck_tails splits at the last `@`, so the
# name keeps its own. The canonical spelling of the same file needs no VFS call at all.
query II
SELECT panduck_format_for('git://icon@2x.md@HEAD')     AS at_name_at_rev,
       panduck_format_for('git://icon@2x.md?ref=HEAD') AS at_name_ref_query;
----
markdown	markdown

# The answer only chooses the reader, so it holds for a file that does not exist.
query I
SELECT panduck_can_read('git://no/such/file.md@HEAD@{0}');
----
true
